                <pb facs="0521" n="401" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89/2a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-03T10:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1922—10
                                a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Repeat following to Prague, Helsingfors, London, Budapest, Rome, Warsaw, and
                    Bucharest: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Reference Department’s circular through Paris, dated April 21, noon,
                            regarding World War Foreign Debt Commission. Report whether the
                            Government to which you are accredited has appointed representatives,
                            and when likely to arrive in Washington. It is desired that negotiations
                            begin at an early date.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
